{"name":"Shearwater Black","hex":"#5b5b6c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shearwater","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the long-winged pelagic seabirds of the family Procellariidae in genera Puffinus, Ardenna, and Calonectris, that breed on islands and coastal cliffs.","Any of the entire family Procellariidae, including certain of the petrels."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shearwater"},{"term":"black","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Absorbing all light and reflecting none; dark and hueless.","Without light."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour/color perceived in the absence of light, but also when no light is reflected, but rather absorbed.","A black dye or pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shearwater","blocks":[{"text":"Shearwaters are medium-sized long-winged seabirds in the petrel family Procellariidae. They have a global marine distribution, but are most common in temperate and cold waters, and are pelagic outside the breeding season."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Puffinus_gravisPCCA20070623-3738B.jpg/330px-Puffinus_gravisPCCA20070623-3738B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shearwater","wikidata":"Q2729486"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black","wikidata":"Q23445"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Cory%27s_Shearwater_%28Calonectris_borealis%29_shearing_in_flight%2C_Corvo_Island%2C_Azores%2C_Portugal.jpg/500px-Cory%27s_Shearwater_%28Calonectris_borealis%29_shearing_in_flight%2C_Corvo_Island%2C_Azores%2C_Portugal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Cory%27s_Shearwater_%28Calonectris_borealis%29_shearing_in_flight%2C_Corvo_Island%2C_Azores%2C_Portugal.jpg/1280px-Cory%27s_Shearwater_%28Calonectris_borealis%29_shearing_in_flight%2C_Corvo_Island%2C_Azores%2C_Portugal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Cory%27s_Shearwater_%28Calonectris_borealis%29_shearing_in_flight%2C_Corvo_Island%2C_Azores%2C_Portugal.jpg/500px-Cory%27s_Shearwater_%28Calonectris_borealis%29_shearing_in_flight%2C_Corvo_Island%2C_Azores%2C_Portugal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cory's shearwater in flight, showing the wingtip 'shearing' the sea surface","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACory's_Shearwater_(Calonectris_borealis)_shearing_in_flight%2C_Corvo_Island%2C_Azores%2C_Portugal.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Yellowstone-black-bear-07895.jpg/500px-Yellowstone-black-bear-07895.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Yellowstone-black-bear-07895.jpg/500px-Yellowstone-black-bear-07895.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":